# Trivy ignore file — springboot-eks-mysql
# Each entry is a finding ID with a documented reason.

# AWS-0040: EKS endpoint_public_access = true
# Required: GitHub Actions CI runners are on public IPs and must reach the
# Kubernetes API to run kubectl/helm during the configure and verify stages.
# Mitigated by: endpoint_private_access=true (in-cluster traffic uses private
# endpoint), KMS Secret encryption, and audit logging on all control-plane logs.
AVD-AWS-0040

# AWS-0041: EKS public_access_cidrs includes 0.0.0.0/0
# GitHub Actions hosted-runner IPs rotate across thousands of Azure datacenter
# ranges and cannot be pinned to a stable CIDR. Restricting to a fixed CIDR
# would break CI on every new runner assignment.
# Mitigated by: IAM/RBAC authentication is still required to access the API;
# the open CIDR only controls network reachability, not authorization.
AVD-AWS-0041

# AWS-0042: EKS node security group allows unrestricted egress (0.0.0.0/0)
# EKS worker nodes require unrestricted outbound access to:
#   - ECR endpoints (image pulls)
#   - AWS APIs (EKS auth, SSM, CloudWatch, STS)
#   - Kubernetes API server (control-plane communication)
# Restricting egress here breaks core EKS functionality.
AVD-AWS-0042
